 "refit %.0f": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "%.0f / %.1fs": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "Your units and their refit classes. DPS = damage per second before armor. T1/T2 = refit tier.": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "Enemy units and allied lane creeps. Crystal armor resists energy; shields regenerate after 3 s without damage.": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "Buildable structures need an engineer; others belong to the map.": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "Damage is first taken by the energy shield (shield column), then by the hull: the hull multiplier for the armor type is applied and flat armor is subtracted (at least 1 damage, except EMP). Area weapons also hit everything nearby on the same layer (ground or air).": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "Damage \\ armor": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "shield": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "kinetic: machine guns - shreds light vehicles, weak against tanks and buildings": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "piercing: cannons - the answer to heavy armor": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "explosive: rockets, mortars, artillery - area damage, best against buildings": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "energy: Void plasma - strong against shields, weak against crystal armor": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "emp: almost no hull damage, but strips shields three times faster": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "Most guns hit only ground targets; aircraft need machine-gun towers, scouts, missiles or flak.": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "Each vehicle has three module slots. Armor opens at Veteran, system and weapon at Elite. A new module replaces the old one in its slot. Modules are visible on the vehicle.": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "%s%s gun: %.0f dmg / %.2fs, range %.1f, %s": "UiGuide.cpp",
 "Refits change a vehicle's class and keep its rank, experience, items and modules. Tier 1 needs Elite, tier 2 needs Hero. You can switch between classes of the same tier or move down the branch.": "UiGuide.cpp",
